WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.633
Weaviate.

2
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:06.433
A vector database with two ideas worth knowing, even if you never deploy it.

3
00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:10.467
Weaviate is a full-featured vector database.

4
00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.973
Its first idea: vectorizer modules.

5
00:00:12.973 --> 00:00:16.000
It embeds your objects and your queries for you.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.067
Its second: hybrid search, with one dial that blends keyword and vector scores.

7
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.700
Let's see the first idea.

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.600
You insert a plain object.

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.800
The collection's embedding model turns it into a vector automatically.

10
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.267
And it lands in the index, with no separate embedding pipeline to write.

11
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.000
At search time, your query is embedded the very same way.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.467
Now the second idea, the alpha dial.

13
00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:45.633
At zero, the search is pure BM25 keyword matching.

14
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.167
At one, it is pure vector similarity.

15
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.067
Anywhere in between blends both, continuously.

16
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.467
Here it is in code.

17
00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:56.767
One query call runs both retrievers at once.

18
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:01.533
Alpha of zero point six leans toward vectors, but keeps some keyword weight.

19
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:04.294
Sweep alpha, and the ranking shifts.

20
00:01:04.294 --> 00:01:07.233
Lexical wins at zero, semantic wins at one.

21
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.833
Here is why this dial is a teaching instrument.

22
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.668
You load a thousand chunks and sweep alpha over twenty eval questions.

23
00:01:15.668 --> 00:01:19.167
Identifier heavy questions peak near zero point three.

24
00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.633
Conceptual questions peak near zero point nine.

25
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:26.129
And the blended set peaks at zero point six five.

26
00:01:26.129 --> 00:01:30.433
Your intuition is now calibrated on your corpus, in one afternoon.

27
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:32.409
Let's recap.

28
00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:35.967
Vectorizer modules embed your data and queries for you.

29
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.633
Hybrid search blends keyword and vector scores in one call.

30
00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.500
Alpha runs from zero, pure keyword, to one, pure vector.

31
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.776
So sweep it on your own eval.

32
00:01:45.776 --> 00:01:46.867
Next up: Milvus.
